PART 1 — PROJECT PURPOSE
1. What is mint-helper?

mint-helper is a free, open-source Linux desktop companion designed primarily for Linux Mint.

The purpose is to make Linux easier for new users and more convenient for experienced users.

After installing Linux Mint, users often need to perform many manual tasks:

Install applications.
Configure a browser.
Install multimedia codecs.
Install additional fonts.
Configure LibreOffice.
Enable the firewall.
Configure automatic updates.
Install developer tools.
Configure their desktop.
Clean unnecessary files.
Configure backups.
Manage Flatpak applications.
Check system information.

mint-helper should bring these tasks together into one modern, simple and reliable application.

The application should be useful beyond the first installation. Users should be able to keep it installed for regular system maintenance and management.

